node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
*.log
.vercel
.netlify

# Design handoff source + duplicate assets — kept locally, not deployed.
# The hero image lives at assets/hero-poster.png; "Tangible Memories 2.png" is
# a byte-identical copy of it (verified by md5), so it stays out of the repo.
*.zip
Tangible Memories 2.png
Hero Image.png

# Gallery source photos + scratch crops. The shipped tiles are assets/session-*.jpg;
# these are the full-size phone originals they were cut from (~1.5MB each) and the
# working files used to find the crop. Kept locally, never committed.
assets/IMG_*.jpg
assets/IMG_*.DNG
assets/_*.png
assets/*_grid.png

# Instagram posts. posts/ is the numbered posting folder (01-NN in posting order,
# written by ../social-kit/make-post.py --pack). These are social artefacts, not
# website assets — they must never be served from the site or bloat the deploy.
# assets/NN-*.jpg is the same set from before the folder existed; harmless, ignored.
posts/
assets/[0-9][0-9]-*.jpg

# Hidden-prints list written by /admin when no Railway Volume is attached.
data/
